    "diagnosis": "Potential pitfalls in overdiagnosis of thymic carcinoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Hassall&rsquo;s corpuscle in a background of small lymphocytes in a patient later confirmed to have thymic hyperplasia. Non-neoplastic thymic epithelium should not be confused with squamous pearls of a well-differentiated/keratinizing squamous carcinoma (liquid-based cytopathology, Pap).",
    "source": "Charles David Sturgis",
    "copyright": "",
