    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Potential pitfalls in overdiagnosis of thymic carcinoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Dispersed bland epithelioid cells and an abortive epithelial whorl in a background of small lymphocytes. The patient was later confirmed to have a B1&nbsp;thymoma. As with non-neoplastic thymic elements, epithelium in thymomas should not be overdiagnosed as thymic carcinoma (Giemsa).",
